'''Visa requirements for [[Argentine nationality law|Argentine citizens]]''' are administrative entry restrictions by the authorities of other states placed on citizens of Argentina.

As of 2026, Argentina citizens had visa-free or visa on arrival access to 168 countries and territories. Ranking the [[Argentine passport]] 15th in terms of travel freedom (tied with the passports of [[Visa requirements for Sammarinese citizens|San Marino]], and tied with the second greatest access of all [[Mercosur#Member states|Mercosur]] single market member states, according to the [[Henley Passport Index]].<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.henleyglobal.com/passport-index/ranking| title=Henley Passport Index Global Ranking | website=Henley & Partners}}</ref>

